      "tier": "standard",
      "headline": "Week 6 Preview: The Magicians Come for the Geeks",
      "body": "Gridiron Geeks own the series 9-4, but Dark Magicians of Chaos won the only playoff meeting and are projected ahead this week. Plus Vitside, Pacific and a winless Maverick that can still bite.",
      "franchiseIds": [],
      "link": "/theleague/news/sf_2026_matchup_preview_w06_v2",
      "linkLabel": "Read matchup preview",
      "league": "theleague",
      "authorId": "claude",
      "content": [
        "<p>Game of the Week: Gridiron Geeks lead this series 9-4, but Dark Magicians of Chaos won the only playoff meeting. Dak Prescott (26.2) and Jayden Daniels (26.0) have the Magicians projected 131.1 to 128.2. I'm taking the upset. Follow it on <a href=\"/theleague/live-scoring\">the live scoreboard</a>.</p>",
        "<p>Vitside Mafia have won the last 3 meetings with Cowboy Up, and Josh Allen (28.6) has them projected 148.1 to 112.9. Make it 4. Pacific Pigskins have won 7 straight and the last 6 against The Mariachi Ninjas. Jared Goff (26.8) keeps both streaks going, 133.0 to 98.2.</p>",
        "<p>Upset alert: Maverick is 0-9 and Da Dangsters have won the last 5 meetings, but Patrick Mahomes (24.0) has Maverick projected 113.1 to 116.7. That is close enough to sweat. Da Dangsters, check <a href=\"/theleague/lineup\">your lineup</a> before kickoff.</p>",
        "<p>Broadcast guide: Cincinnati is the must-watch, with Joe Burrow, Ja'Marr Chase, Tee Higgins and Chase Brown spread across four teams. Detroit is next, with Jared Goff, Jahmyr Gibbs, Sam LaPorta and Amon-Ra St. Brown. Set your multiview on <a href=\"/theleague/sunday-ticket\">the Sunday Ticket board</a>, then live on <a href=\"/theleague/live-scoring\">the scoreboard</a>.</p>"
      ],
